course: dictionary
lesson: 6776
title: Optical: seeing and light
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word optical is about seeing and light. It means to do with the eyes, or with light and how it travels. In «optical illusion», the picture tricks your eyes and brain, so optical must be about seeing.
explain: Use the words around it as clues. In «Optical fibres are thin strands of glass that carry light along bends», the clue is carry light, so optical fibres must be about light. Check by swapping in a meaning: "to do with light" fits «optical fibres», and "to do with seeing" fits «optical illusion».
fact: «Optical» means to do with seeing and the eyes, or with light and how it travels.
fact: «Optically» is the adverb form, meaning in a way that relates to seeing or light.
fact: An optical illusion is a picture that tricks your eyes and brain.
fact: An optical fibre is a thin glass thread that carries light, and most of the internet travels through such fibres.
fact: Optical instruments, such as lenses, microscopes and telescopes, use light to help us see.
exercise: «Light can travel along thin glass threads, called optical fibres.» What does optical mean in optical fibres? | Very heavy and hard to move | *To do with light and how it travels | To do with cooking food
exercise: «The eye sees, but the brain guesses what it is seeing and can be fooled, as in optical illusions.» What is an optical illusion? | A thin glass thread that carries light | A kind of pet fish | *A picture that tricks your eyes and brain
exercise: What do opticians sell? | Books | *Glasses | Shoes | Bread
test: «The picture looked real, but optically it was a trick.» What does optically mean here? | In a slow and careful way | In a loud and noisy way | *In a way that fools the eyes
test: Which of these is an optical instrument, one that uses lenses and light? | A pillow | A bicycle bell | A spoon | *A telescope
exam: «An optical mouse gets lost on clear glass with no pattern to see.» Why does it get lost? | It ran out of batteries | It was switched on in the wrong room | *Its camera has no pattern to take pictures of
